<http://classif-mcp.local/unsd/coicop2018/07.3.2.1/note/inclusionNote> a xkos:ExplanatoryNote ;
    xkos:plainText "* transport of persons and accompanied luggage by bus, trolleybus, and coach_x000D_\n* transport of persons and accompanied luggage by share taxi, a vehicle for hire that may be characterized as a cross between a taxicab and a bus. This mode of transport is often utilized in developing countries. Share taxis are typically smaller in size than buses, ranging from four-seat cars to minibuses, and are often owner-operated. They usually operate without a timetable along a fixed or semi-fixed route and may stop anywhere along that route to pick up or drop off passengers."@en .

